WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.560
A fungus lives in a plant's roots.

2
00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.720
Is it a friend or a freeloader?

3
00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.040
You cannot tell by looking.

4
00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:13.520
So how would you find out?

5
00:00:14.483 --> 00:00:18.243
Measure each partner's fitness, its survival and reproduction.

6
00:00:19.703 --> 00:00:23.363
Then compare it with the same organism living without the partner.

7
00:00:24.563 --> 00:00:26.743
The difference is the partner's net effect.

8
00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:29.393
Picture a balance.

9
00:00:30.693 --> 00:00:33.533
On one side sits the benefit the partner brings.

10
00:00:34.913 --> 00:00:36.713
On the other sits the cost it takes.

11
00:00:38.333 --> 00:00:39.813
Benefit minus cost is the net.

12
00:00:40.833 --> 00:00:43.353
The sign of that net names the interaction.

13
00:00:44.813 --> 00:00:47.033
Both partners gain: mutualism.

14
00:00:48.233 --> 00:00:51.793
One gains, the other shows no net change: commensalism.

15
00:00:52.993 --> 00:00:55.573
One gains, the other loses: parasitism.

16
00:00:56.767 --> 00:00:58.927
Now load the balance for a root fungus.

17
00:01:00.247 --> 00:01:02.067
The fungus takes carbon from the plant.

18
00:01:03.267 --> 00:01:08.267
That is the cost. It supplies soil nutrients, especially phosphorus.

19
00:01:09.747 --> 00:01:10.747
That is the benefit.

20
00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:16.910
In this sketch, phosphorus starts scarce, so the fungus's delivery is worth a lot.

21
00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:19.850
The benefit outweighs the cost.

22
00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:22.550
The plant's net is positive.

23
00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:26.143
Now add phosphorus until it is plentiful.

24
00:01:27.603 --> 00:01:29.803
Suppose the carbon cost stays the same.

25
00:01:31.083 --> 00:01:32.383
Where does the plant's net go?

26
00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:42.280
The benefit shrinks, because phosphorus is no longer scarce.

27
00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:45.760
In this sketch, the net slides through zero.

28
00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:48.920
The same fungus now costs the plant.

29
00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:55.190
If the fungus still gains, the pair has moved from mutualism toward parasitism.

30
00:01:56.590 --> 00:02:00.050
Ecologists call this the mutualism-parasitism continuum.

31
00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:03.210
Where a pair sits depends on conditions.

32
00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.280
A net of zero needs care too.

33
00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:10.120
A large benefit and a large cost can cancel.

34
00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:13.920
A level balance can still be carrying heavy loads.

35
00:02:15.033 --> 00:02:18.173
The partner's own traits load the balance as well.

36
00:02:19.553 --> 00:02:23.973
Rhizobia are bacteria in legume root nodules, small swellings on the roots.

37
00:02:25.213 --> 00:02:28.513
They fix nitrogen from the air and take carbon in return.

38
00:02:29.583 --> 00:02:32.843
Now picture a strain that takes carbon but skips the fixing.

39
00:02:34.123 --> 00:02:37.443
It could leave more offspring than an honest strain, and spread.

40
00:02:38.783 --> 00:02:39.783
What stops it?

41
00:02:40.683 --> 00:02:42.803
One answer is a host sanction.

42
00:02:44.003 --> 00:02:48.383
The host cuts the reproduction of rhizobia in nodules that do not fix.

43
00:02:49.683 --> 00:02:52.023
That puts a new weight on the cheater's cost side.

44
00:02:53.033 --> 00:02:54.733
Now let the partners evolve.

45
00:02:55.933 --> 00:03:00.433
A change in one shifts the other's balance, so selection on the other changes.

46
00:03:01.733 --> 00:03:05.093
If the other then evolves in response, that is coevolution.

47
00:03:06.667 --> 00:03:08.747
Daniel Janzen set this standard.

48
00:03:10.107 --> 00:03:13.027
A good fit between two species is not the evidence.

49
00:03:14.287 --> 00:03:15.807
Change in both partners is.

50
00:03:17.817 --> 00:03:21.397
So an interaction's sign is not a label fixed to a species.

51
00:03:22.817 --> 00:03:26.817
Each partner's side is a net, measured against life without the partner.

52
00:03:28.197 --> 00:03:29.417
Conditions can move it.
